 Breeze support Push CDN?'=>'Does Breeze support Push CDN?','Amazon Cloudfront'=>'Amazon Cloudfront','KeyCDN'=>'KeyCDN','MaxCDN'=>'MaxCDN','Breeze supports the following three popular CDNs:'=>'Breeze supports the following three popular CDNs:','What popular CDN are supported by Breeze Plugin?'=>'What popular CDN are supported by Breeze Plugin?','Yes, Breeze Plugin is compatible with Visual Builder.'=>'Yes, Breeze Plugin is compatible with Visual Builder.','Pingdom'=>'Pingdom','WebPagetest'=>'WebPagetest','Google Page Speed'=>'Google Page Speed','You will be able to see the impact of the Breeze Cache Plugin almost immediately. We also recommend using the following tools for generating metrics:'=>'You will be able to see the impact of the Breeze Cache Plugin almost immediately. We also recommend using the following tools for generating metrics:','You can get your questions answered on the WordPress support forums. If you are a Cloudways customer, please feel free to start a discussion at'=>'You can get your questions answered on the WordPress support forums. If you are a Cloudways customer, please feel free to start a discussion at','Where can I get support for Breeze?'=>'Where can I get support for Breeze?','Does it work with all hosting providers?'=>'Does it work with all hosting providers?','this KB to exclude URLs from the Varnish cache.'=>'this KB to exclude URLs from the Varnish cache.','If Varnish is active, you will need to exclude URLs and file type(s) in the Varnish configuration. If you are hosting WordPress websites on Cloudways servers, follow '=>'If Varnish is active, you will need to exclude URLs and file type(s) in the Varnish configuration. If you are hosting WordPress websites on Cloudways servers, follow ','Can I exclude URLs of individual files and pages from cache?'=>'Can I exclude URLs of individual files and pages from cache?','Comments will appear upon moderation as per the comment system (or policy) set in place by the blog owner. Other dynamic changes such as any modifications in files will require a full cache purge.'=>'Comments will appear upon moderation as per the comment system (or policy) set in place by the blog owner. Other dynamic changes such as any modifications in files will require a full cache purge.','Will comments and other dynamic parts of my blog appear immediately?'=>'Will comments and other dynamic parts of my blog appear immediately?','WordPress databases are notorious for storing information like post revisions, spam comments and much more. Over time, databases l become bloated and it is a good practice to clear out unwanted information to reduce database size and improve optimization.'=>'WordPress databases are notorious for storing information like post revisions, spam comments and much more. Over time, databases l become bloated and it is a good practice to clear out unwanted information to reduce database size and improve optimisation.','What does Breeze\'s Database Optimization feature do?'=>'What does Breeze\'s Database Optimisation feature do?','Breeze supports CDN integration. It allows all static assets (such as images, CSS and JS files) to be served via CDN.'=>'Breeze supports CDN integration. It allows all static assets (such as images, CSS and JS files) to be served via CDN.','Does Breeze support CDN?'=>'Does Breeze support CDN?','Does Breeze have compatibility issues with other known plugins?'=>'Does Breeze have compatibility issues with other known plugins?','Breeze does not require any special configuration to work with HTTP or HTTPS pages.'=>'Breeze does not require any special configuration to work with HTTP or HTTPS pages.','Is Breeze compatible with HTTPS?'=>'Is Breeze compatible with HTTPS?','We strongly recommend that you use Breeze as the only cache plugin for your website. If there are any other cache plugins installed, please ensure that you have disabled them prior to proceeding with the Breeze installation.'=>'We strongly recommend that you use Breeze as t